; Stage 15 B3′ — the did-you-mean tier of `unknown-type-message`, executed.
;
; B3′ gave `unknown-type-message` the same tier order `unresolved-name-message`
; has (out-of-scope qualifier → unreachable definer → other namespace →
; did-you-mean). This fixture exists to RUN the last tier: it is a cold error
; path, and conventions.md's fixed-arity rule is that a format helper called with
; the wrong number of arguments on a path nothing executes is invisible forever.
; The first cut of that line called `fmt-3s` with two arguments; the Stage 15 W9
; call-arity check caught it at `make bootstrap`, and this keeps it caught.
(defstruct Widget n:i32)

(defn b3-take ((w (ref Widgat))):i32 (return (_get w n)))

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
